+% A variable shared by the input and output space is ONE variable and must   % MMP, 09/09/2026
+% carry one interval: delta(s-s') in a multiplier direction identifies the   % MMP, 09/09/2026
+% two copies, and the bounds of an integral direction come from a single     % MMP, 09/09/2026
+% interval. Callers generated dom.in and dom.out independently, so a shared  % MMP, 09/09/2026
+% variable got two intervals; the sopvar constructor now rejects that. The   % MMP, 09/09/2026
+% input side is taken as authoritative. Done here rather than in each caller % MMP, 09/09/2026
+% because this routine may generate the variable names itself, in which case % MMP, 09/09/2026
+% no caller can align them.                                                  % MMP, 09/09/2026
+vS3_dom = intersect(vars.in,vars.out);                                      % MMP, 09/09/2026
+if ~isempty(vS3_dom)                                                        % MMP, 09/09/2026
+    [~,i_in ] = ismember(vS3_dom,vars.in);                                  % MMP, 09/09/2026
+    [~,i_out] = ismember(vS3_dom,vars.out);                                 % MMP, 09/09/2026
+    dom.out(i_out,:) = dom.in(i_in,:);                                      % MMP, 09/09/2026
+end                                                                         % MMP, 09/09/2026
